config MT7932_FULLMAC
	tristate "MediaTek MT7932 Wi-Fi on the Apple MacBook Neo (J700)"
	depends on PCI && OF && ARM64 && IOMMU_DMA
	depends on PCIE_APPLE_T8140_BOOTSTRAP && CFG80211
	select FW_LOADER
	select CRYPTO
	select CRYPTO_HMAC
	select CRYPTO_SHA1
	select CRYPTO_LIB_SHA256
	help
	  Support for the Wi-Fi function of the MediaTek MT7932 radio in the
	  Apple MacBook Neo (J700). The firmware runs association and the
	  WPA2-PSK, WPA3-SAE or OWE handshake. The driver is a cfg80211 station
	  on 2.4 GHz, 5 GHz UNII-1/2/2e/3 and country-permitted 6 GHz UNII-5..8.
	  6 GHz requires SAE-H2E or OWE, MFP and country VLP power data.
	  Radar (DFS) channels are scanned passively; an AP heard there
	  during the connect attempt may be joined, and is left when it
	  announces a channel switch. Other MediaTek devices and other
	  machines are not matched.

	  The driver needs the original firmware, the unit's own calibration
	  and the country policy packages under mediatek/mt7932/, besides the
	  cfg80211 regulatory database. The device is probed before the root
	  filesystem is mounted, so say M unless those files are in the
	  initramfs.

	  Once the device has been given DMA addresses, the module cannot be
	  unloaded. A function that fails to initialize and cannot be reset
	  stays bound and keeps its DMA memory.

config MT7932_AWDL
	bool "Experimental clean-room MT7932 AWDL interface"
	depends on MT7932_FULLMAC
	default n
	help
	  Build the experimental second-BSS Apple Wireless Direct Link path.
	  It exposes an awdl0 station-typed Ethernet interface, programs the native
	  firmware AWDL command records and routes BSS-1 RX records.  The option
	  is deliberately off by default while firmware policy values and target
	  validation remain incomplete.
	  Systems using NetworkManager should install 80-mt7932-awdl.rules from
	  this directory into /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/ before loading the driver,
	  so only the AWDL controller brings awdl0 up.

config MT7932_AWDL_KUNIT_TEST
	bool "KUnit tests for MT7932 AWDL records and RX parsing" if !KUNIT_ALL_TESTS
	depends on KUNIT=y && MT7932_AWDL
	default KUNIT_ALL_TESTS
	help
	  Test every clean-room command-record builder, AWDL data framing and
	  synthetic CONNAC2/event receive records without radio hardware.
	  Check station routing and BSS activation/rollback command submission.

config MT7932_RF_KUNIT_TEST
	bool "KUnit tests for MT7932 terminal RF failure" if !KUNIT_ALL_TESTS
	depends on KUNIT=y && MT7932_FULLMAC
	default KUNIT_ALL_TESTS
	help
	  Exercise the driver's terminal calibration failure and startup
	  admission paths with synthetic devices, without radio hardware.
	  Check association wakeups, retained peer ownership and refusal to
	  reopen RF admission after a terminal calibration error.
	  Check that a connection whose AP the firmware lost is ended.

config MT7932_KUNIT_TEST
	bool "KUnit tests for MT7932 firmware input validation" if !KUNIT_ALL_TESTS
	depends on KUNIT=y && MT7932_FULLMAC
	default KUNIT_ALL_TESTS
	help
	  Exercise the validation of what the firmware and the device hand
	  to the driver, with synthetic, truncated and corrupted input and
	  without radio hardware: receive descriptors, including frames the
	  hardware did not decrypt, command replies, regulatory snapshots
	  and country power packages. Also check connection admission, SAE
	  request encoding, WPA passphrase derivation, channel switch
	  announcements and what is reported when a move to another AP
	  lands, fails or is cancelled.
